# Generated and machine-local parts of the layout editor.
#
# Only what is rebuilt on demand, or is not ours to ship, is ignored. Anything
# the editor needs as *input* is kept however large: the point of this folder is
# that anyone can clone it and build a ship without hunting down assets.

# Module thumbnails and turntable renders, rebuilt by the server on first
# request, plus its own logs. ~51 MB.
tool/cache/

# Saved layouts are scratch copies; the ship the tool actually reloads is
# export/ship_manifest.json.
tool/layouts/

# Each suite drops a screenshot at the end of its run, purely to be looked at.
# Tracked once, they turned into binary churn in every diff: `npm test`
# rewrites all three whether or not anything changed.
tool/test/shot-*.png

# The exported ship: a 31 MB .glb rebuilt from the manifest by "Export glb",
# and the timestamped manifest backups the server keeps on every save. The
# live manifest itself is NOT ignored - it is the ship.
export/*.glb
export/ship_manifest.*-*.json

# The HDRI is a placeholder with no recorded provenance, and is not the one this
# ship will ship with - so it is not committed. The editor starts without it and
# says so ("no HDRI, metals will look flat"); only reflections suffer, because
# metals take nearly all their brightness from the IBL. Drop any .hdr in here
# and point ENV_HDRI (tool/public/js/editor.js) at it.
env/*.hdr

# Deliberately NOT ignored, despite the size:
#   kit/  35 MB of CC0 modules - see license.txt. Bundled so the editor runs
#         anywhere without a separate download.